# framecite — per-frame mini references for beamer + biblatex

Version 0.8, released 2026/11/20.

framecite shows the sources cited on a beamer slide as a small block at
the bottom of that same slide, so the audience sees where a claim comes
from without leaving the slide. Each entry prints the citation label in
the active biblatex style, the author (or editor), and the quoted title.
The block sits between real LaTeX footnotes and the theme footline;
entries appear in order of first citation, deduplicated per frame.
Collection is automatic from the standard cite commands; manual
registration (`\fcite`) and blind registration (`\fsource`) are available.

Requirements: a beamer document, and biblatex loaded before framecite
(etoolbox and xspace are loaded automatically; titles are quoted via
biblatex's `mkbibquote`, so loading `csquotes` is optional --- load it
with any options wherever you like for language-aware quotation marks).

Full documentation: `framecite.pdf`.

Build the package and the manual from the sources:

    pdflatex framecite.ins     # generates framecite.sty
    latexmk -pdf framecite.dtx  # or: pdflatex; makeindex; pdflatex x2

Alternatively use `l3build`:

    l3build unpack   # framecite.sty
    l3build doc      # framecite.pdf
    l3build ctan     # upload zip for CTAN

